I hear that Valkyries are the most common first ascensions, and
apparently the RNG thought it might as well let me add one more to the
list. I'm not terribly good at Nethack, as I've only been playing it
for maybe eight months, but I did get terribly lucky.

By DL2 or 3, the game was looking pretty good. Censored (not my
Valkyrie's _actual_ name; I created her right after the Troll-related
choking death of my previous very good game, currently occupying the
5th place of my high score list- it was the first decent game I'd had
in two or three months) found a pair of Gauntlets of Power just lying
around on the floor, and the game just went from there. Got a wish
from a lamp, also found lying around, and decided that some grey
dragon scale would be in order. Got down to Mine Town and had not much
to do- the altar wasn't mine, and there wasn't too much great in the
shops. Looted Mine's End, then went back up and converted my longsword
into the +1 rustproof Excalibur (which, I must say, came in very handy
throughout the game, between its auto-searching and its level-drain
resistance). Went through Sokoban next, ending up with an amulet of
reflection, nicely complementing my armor.

I Converted three altars as I proceeded downstairs; used them to make
maybe 10 holy waters, and after much wheedling, cajoling, and outright
begging, Tyr decided I was cool enough to be given Mjolnir. Thus
armed, I headed down to Medusa, blindfold, ring of levitation, and
oilskin cloak in hand, slaughtering the foul beast in about three
hits. Got down to the castle a few minutes later, blew apart the
drawbridge, froze the moat, killed several things, and then noticed,
lo and behold, I was level 14! So I went and stole the Orb of Fate
from Lord Surtur. Somewhere along the way I fought a Lich and decided
that enemies that cursed my stuff and summoned more opponents weren't
high on my list of things I'd like to be seeing, so I got rid of 'em
all. Headed back to the castle to kill off the rest of its
inhabitants, claim my wand of wishing, get an amulet of life saving
(at this point, I didn't have many other ideas of what to wish for-
speed boots would've been good, but I thought of those later on), and
kill and eat a black dragon for disintegration resistance (because,
you know, just in _case_).

The Valley of the Dead and Gehennom went very easily, aside from some
troublesome Demon Lords. I really don't understand how you're supposed
to kill an enemy that teleports away to heal, then runs up the stairs
when you chase it- unless there's a handy cockatrice corpse nearby,
which there was, or maybe a wand of death would work, I suppose. So I
found the way up to Rodney's tower, for the first non-explore mode
game ever, and thought "What the heck? I'll kill him. Probably this
game won't last much longer either way.", and so I did. And realized
that I didn't have the Bell. On my way to visit Vlad, I realized that,
in addition to the Bell, I was missing three candles- forgot to buy
some in Mine Town. So I killed Vlad and took his Bell, then decided
that since I didn't have anything too critical to wish for, I'd just
waste the a wish on three candles.
I would have wished for more amulets of life saving, but I'd found
three more just lying on the ground. I kid you not.

I found the Vibrating Square fairly easily (thank god- last time I
tried, in explore mode, it took me something like a half hour), went
and got the Amulet, and started back up the stairs. For about ten
minutes, two out of three staircases I tried would teleport me back
down at least one level, but after that they calmed down and I made it
up to DL1 with no event. Dug my way through the Plane of Earth rather
quickly, and then got killed once, nearly twice, by Air Elementals on
the next Plane, before I thought to put on my ring of conflict. Fire
and Water went even easier than Earth, and before I knew it I was
standing on the Astral Plane. The first temple I checked wasn't, as
nearly as I could determine (because I figured I could tell from the
priests inside- whoops) mine, so I evaded Famine and headed quickly to
the next. This time, I checked the altar, and found it definitely
wasn't mine- but Famine and Pestilence didn't want me to leave, and it
took me dying twice before I could get away. Headed over to the last
temple (even though the first one still might've been mine), narrowly
avoiding death by Death, and got inside... to find that I was,
wouldn't you know it, blind- and thus unable to tell which altar I was
standing on. So I locked the door closed to wait my blindness out,
until a giant bashed it in; Death nearly came inside before I pushed
the boulder the giant had left behind into the doorway. I waited and
waited, in increments of 100 turns, for my blindness to go away. Ate a
carrot; didn't help. Getting desperate, I turned to folks online for
an answer, any method to cure my ailing vision- and then realized, to
my chagrin, that I ought to take the towel off my head.

Really, it's amazing I ascended at all, between my lack of common
sense and the status of my character- when I reached Tyr's altar, I
was level 19, with 221 hit points, and an AC of a mere -25. I didn't
polypile, genocided only 1 class of monsters (4 species), and my
wishes (if I remember correctly) were for a few blessed scrolls of
charging, my gray dragon scale, a BoH, an amulet of life saving, some
candles, and some scrolls of remove curse (upon reaching the vibrating
square)- and, I believe, some scrolls of identify at one point
(because I got mind-flayered a bit, and though I had some identify on
me I had no idea whatsoever what it was anymore). Didn't nurse-dance,
pudding-farm, or even really stand around sacrificing too much-
basically, I avoided all of the things I've generally been told will
lead to a sure ascension. But, hey, I can't complain- the RNG must
like me. ^_^

